    ...sec('edge cases worth knowing'),
    ...bullet('Unwritable cache', 'an unwritable XDG_CACHE_HOME or XDG_STATE_HOME gives an E739 from init.lua or lazy.nvim.'),
    ...bullet('Tool lock', 'clippy waits while another cargo holds the package-cache lock under the cargo home.'),
    ...bullet('Large files', 'typing hitches in a 1 MB, 50k-line Rust file; the cause was not found.'),
    ...bullet('Offline', 'kulala’s first scripted request waits for an npm install and a rollup build, about 70 seconds, and needs network.'),
    ...sec('how it is tested'),
    ...text('The items in this file are not tests themselves. tests/COVERAGE.md says a bug a spec finds is written as an assertion of the correct behaviour, skipped while it reproduces, and that the bugs found so far are fixed. The platform skips are real code: specs carry xyno-os headers that skip a whole file on an operating system with a printed reason, and H.known_issue marks undiagnosed failures; the scripts-portable spec has cases for the header skip and for H.need_os and H.need_posix. Nothing in this file is checked automatically for staleness, which is the one real weakness of the format.'),
